IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ppl-logic`
IMPORT `ppl-time`

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425, Chapter 2 Part 2-3 Division 4 Subdivision A (sections 37 to 40):
-- the income test. The limits themselves (section 41) and their indexation (sections 42 to 44) are in ppl-time.
-- Adjusted taxable income is worked out under another Act's Schedule, so it is asked as an input.
-- Income years are asked as inputs: the text borrows that term without defining it.

-- src:876 | A person’s adjusted taxable income for an income year is worked out in accordance with Schedule 3 to the Family Assistance Act (disregarding subclause 2(2) and clauses 3 and 3A of that Schedule).
@ref s 38 (src:876-876)
GIVEN `the amount worked out under Schedule 3 to the Family Assistance Act, disregarding subclause 2(2) and clauses 3 and 3A of that Schedule` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a person's adjusted taxable income for an income year` MEANS
    `the amount worked out under Schedule 3 to the Family Assistance Act, disregarding subclause 2(2) and clauses 3 and 3A of that Schedule`

-- src:879 | The reference income year for a person is:
-- src:880 | (a) the income year that ended before the earlier of:
-- src:881 | (i) the day the person made the claim; and
-- src:882 | (ii) the day the child was born.
@ref s 39 (src:879-882)
GIVEN `the day the person made the claim` IS A DATE
      `the day the child was born` IS A DATE
      `the end days of the income years` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the end day of the reference income year for a person` MEANS
    `the end day of the reference income year` (`the earlier of the claim day and the birth day` `the day the person made the claim` `the day the child was born`) `the end days of the income years`

-- src:884 | (1) The relevant individual PPL income limit for a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the individual PPL income limit that applies on the earlier of the following days:
-- src:885 | (a) the day the person made the claim;
-- src:886 | (b) the day the child was born.
@ref s 40(1) (src:884-886)
GIVEN `the day the person made the claim` IS A DATE
      `the day the child was born` IS A DATE
      quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the relevant individual PPL income limit` MEANS
    `the individual PPL income limit that applies on a day` (`the earlier of the claim day and the birth day` `the day the person made the claim` `the day the child was born`) quarters

-- src:887 | (2) The relevant family PPL income limit for a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the family PPL income limit that applies on the earlier of the following days:
-- src:888 | (a) the day the person made the claim;
-- src:889 | (b) the day the child was born.
@ref s 40(2) (src:887-889)
GIVEN `the day the person made the claim` IS A DATE
      `the day the child was born` IS A DATE
      quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the relevant family PPL income limit` MEANS
    `the family PPL income limit that applies on a day` (`the earlier of the claim day and the birth day` `the day the person made the claim` `the day the child was born`) quarters

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, limit IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an amount is not more than a limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST l THEN JUST (amount AT MOST l)

-- src:857 | (1) A person satisfies the income test on a day:
-- src:858 | (a) that is a flexible PPL day for a child of the person; or
-- src:859 | (b) on which a conditional eligibility determination or initial eligibility determination is made in relation to the person;
-- src:860 | if the person’s adjusted taxable income for the reference income year is not more than the relevant individual PPL income limit.
-- src:861 | (2) A person satisfies the income test on a day:
-- src:862 | (a) that is a flexible PPL day for a child of the person; or
-- src:863 | (b) on which a conditional eligibility determination or initial eligibility determination is made in relation to the person;
-- src:864 | if:
-- src:865 | (c) the person does not have a partner at the time the person makes the claim to which that flexible PPL day or determination relates; and
-- src:866 | (d) the person’s adjusted taxable income for the reference income year is not more than the relevant family PPL income limit.
-- src:867 | (3) A person satisfies the income test on a day:
-- src:868 | (a) that is a flexible PPL day for a child of the person; or
-- src:869 | (b) on which a conditional eligibility determination or initial eligibility determination is made in relation to the person;
-- src:870 | if:
-- src:871 | (c) the person has a partner at the time the person makes the claim to which that flexible PPL day or determination relates; and
-- src:872 | (d) the total of the following amounts is not more than the relevant family PPL income limit:
-- src:873 | (i) the person’s adjusted taxable income for the reference income year;
-- src:874 | (ii) the adjusted taxable income of the person’s partner for the reference income year.
@ref s 37 (src:857-874)
GIVEN `the day is a flexible PPL day for a child of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a conditional eligibility determination or an initial eligibility determination is made in relation to the person on the day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a partner at the time the person makes the claim to which the day or the determination relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year` IS A NUMBER
      `the partner's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year` IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant individual PPL income limit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the relevant family PPL income limit` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a person satisfies the income test on a day` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the day is a flexible PPL day for a child of the person` OR `a conditional eligibility determination or an initial eligibility determination is made in relation to the person on the day`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `either result holds`
             (`an amount is not more than a limit` `the person's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year` `the relevant individual PPL income limit`)
             (`an amount is not more than a limit`
                  (IF `the person has a partner at the time the person makes the claim to which the day or the determination relates`
                   THEN (`the person's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year` PLUS `the partner's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year`)
                   ELSE `the person's adjusted taxable income for the reference income year`)
                  `the relevant family PPL income limit`)

-- src:918 | (4) Amounts are to be worked out under this section:
-- src:919 | (a) using only the index numbers published in terms of the most recently published reference base for the Consumer Price Index; and
-- src:920 | (b) disregarding index numbers published in substitution for previously published index numbers (except where the substituted numbers are published to take account of changes in the reference base).
@ref s 43(4) (src:918-920)
GIVEN `the index number is published in terms of the most recently published reference base for the Consumer Price Index` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the index number is published in substitution for a previously published index number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substituted number is published to take account of changes in the reference base` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`an index number is used in working out an amount under section 43` MEANS
    JUST (        `the index number is published in terms of the most recently published reference base for the Consumer Price Index`
          AND (   (NOT `the index number is published in substitution for a previously published index number`)
               OR `the substituted number is published to take account of changes in the reference base`))
